job.snippet:
Discover your exciting role
Our people are our success. As one of us, you will contribute to engineering excellence for the high-tech markets of the future, including semiconductors, batteries, pharmaceuticals, biotechnology, and data centers. At Exyte, you will be part of a global community of challenge seekers who are ambitious and passionate about innovation. Together, we will build on our company’s long history and keep on leading the way to a better world.
Explore Your Tasks And Responsibilities
Purpose
Responsible for the technical aspects of a particular assigned job to achieve a correct, complete and coordinated design deliverables (ie. calculations, drawings, specifications, reports, etc…);
Assists Lead/Senior piping engineer in achieving project completion within budget and on schedule;
Works independently or with Lead/Senior Engineer in the detailed design;
To plan, monitor and track the day-to-day engineering activities and contractor’s site progress;
Responsibilities
Assists in the preparation and maintaining the Project job file, data books, drawings, specification lists, lists of required design data and design change notices;
Assists in preparing Piping material specifications, pipe stress, pipe support specifications
Assists in preparing Plot plan and Equipment layout drawings;
Prepare / Review Piping General Arrangement drawings;
Prepare / Review isometric drawings and vessel trim drawings;
Prepares Tie-in List and Tie-in Location plan;
Performs pipe stress analysis for critical lines;
Review of standard Pipe support and Piping detail drawings;
Conducts material take-offs and compile Piping Bill of material;
Prepares material requisition for Manual valve, Bulk Pipe/fitting and Specialty item;
Assists in preparation of Piping subcontract requisition.
Show Your Expertise
Professional experience & education-
 Degree in Engineering
 At least 5 years of relevant experience
Specific skills & knowledge (e.g. language skills)-
Design and construction experience in Petrochemical, Refinery and chemical industry preferred
Experience in Plant Design and Piping engineering works
Basic understanding of Equipment/Piping layout and space management
Contact
You want to be part of the Exyte team? We look forward to receiving your application!
For further questions and information, please do not hesitate to contact Shira Shemla via E-Mail at Jobs.il@exyte.net.
Please note that we only consider applications submitted through our application portal. Applications sent via email will not be considered due to data protection regulations.

